        "collapsible_tab_mjEF8T": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is StrideBack™?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>You're giving your dog the one chew that was <strong>built for conservative CCL recovery</strong>, not another everything-chew. Five research-backed actives, one soft daily treat.</p><ul><li>Their healing knee gets what it needs: piperine drives absorption where blood supply is weakest</li><li>The rebuild finally outpaces the damage: glucosamine + chondroitin work while the enzymes slow down</li><li>Progress stops falling apart: curcumin (95% curcuminoids) calms the immune overreaction</li><li>The other knee stays safe: green lipped mussel and hemp seed cushion the leg doing double duty</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_gBgAbF": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why you need it",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>You've watched them hesitate at the stairs. Heard the little cry when they stand up. And everyone keeps telling you surgery is the only way, at $4,000 to $10,000 you may not have.</p><p>Here's what nobody explained: the CCL has <strong>the worst blood supply in your dog's entire body</strong>. Nutrients can't reach it, the immune system attacks the new collagen, and enzymes strip it out faster than it rebuilds. That cycle is why months of generic glucosamine change nothing.</p><p>StrideBack™ was formulated around that cycle: delivery, rebuild, calm, protection. All four fronts, every day.</p><p><strong>You're not failing your dog by skipping surgery. You just needed something built for the road you chose.</strong></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_akEwJj": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Benefits ✨",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>✓ <strong>Hear the morning cry fade</strong>: the actives reach the ligament thanks to piperine-boosted absorption</p><p>✓ <strong>See weight shift back onto the leg</strong>: glucosamine + chondroitin rebuild while enzyme damage slows</p><p>✓ <strong>Watch progress stick, week over week</strong>: curcumin calms the immune flare-ups that undo it</p><p>✓ <strong>Stop bracing for the second tear</strong>: omega-rich green lipped mussel and hemp seed protect the loaded knee</p><p>✓ <strong>Skip the pill fights</strong>: one soft, tasty chew a day, every size and life stage</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_MTCgw9": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to give it (10 seconds a day)",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p><strong>1.</strong> Give the chews with breakfast, dosed by weight (small dogs 1, medium 2, large 3).</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Keep it daily. The rebuild cycle needs consistency, not perfection.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Watch for the small wins: steadier mornings, longer walks, weight back on the leg.</p><p>Works alongside crate rest, braces, and whatever plan you and your vet have chosen.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_FPPE7p": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
